      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Meaning\n\nOne renderable representation. Encoding: a `view` node. A Surface names a track of these representations; a host selects a compatible View within that track."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-view",
          "nodeId": "view-meaning"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "view-invariants",
      "label": "Invariants",
      "type": "content",
      "position": {
        "x": 120,
        "y": -440
      },
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 660,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Invariants\n\nA View may render glyph-shaped artwork without being an icon View. It is still a View representation. Every authored Surface starts with at least one View and ends in its ordinary Glyph; the terminal Glyph does not replace the View.\n\nA View can be shared by more than one valid track. Its geometry and resolution requirement are distinct from the owning graph frame. Graph-facing presentation and the Declaration node’s own class presentation have different owners."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-view",
          "nodeId": "view-invariants"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "view-contract",
      "label": "Contract",
      "type": "content",
      "position": {
        "x": -1000,
        "y": 300
      },
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 660,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Contract\n\n`data.view` describes intent, payload and optional name/enabled state. Payload names such as node.web.detail and editor.web identify web-host intent; they are not a fixed three-step ontology. `data.semanticZoom.resolution` participates in continuous selection. A View owns data.content or delegates to Content. Existing role/payload aliases remain readable."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-view",
          "nodeId": "view-contract"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "view-ports",
      "label": "Ports and Relationships",
      "type": "content",
      "position": {
        "x": 120,
        "y": 300
      },
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 660,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
