        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Behavior\n\n## Implemented behavior\n\nviewResolution computes continuous requirements and selects a fitting entry; viewSequence resolves names and fallbacks. surfaceChains scopes candidates and glyphs to a selected Surface; graphViewPresentation uses that selection. A disabled View is unavailable to resolvers that honor availability. Host/payload selection is not camera control.\n\n## Known gaps\n\nGraph presentation and node-class presentation still have separate callers. The dedicated Declaration renderer and full host/3D integration remain tracked in github://twilite-zone/public/tasks/declaration-surfaces/root.node. Do not claim uniform dispatch merely because the shared resolver exists.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNo additional decision is required to describe the behavior above. Changes to that contract require an explicit task; implementation gaps are not implied approvals.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource (twilite repository):\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/viewResolution.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/viewSequence.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/surfaceChains.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/graphViewPresentation.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/components/WorkspaceLayer.js`\n\nFocused tests (twilite repository):\n- `tests/viewResolution.test.js`\n- `tests/viewSequence.test.js`\n- `tests/graphViewPresentation.test.js`\n- `tests/workspaceCamera.test.js`\n\nThese pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-view",
          "nodeId": "view-behavior"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "view-representations",
      "label": "Representations",
      "type": "content",
      "position": {
        "x": 120,
        "y": 1040
      },
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 660,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          }
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "view.content"
          },
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Representations\n\nA selected representation uses the existing workspace frame. Surface, resolution and focus changes do not implicitly resize it, reflow neighbors or change camera zoom. Manual resizing is explicit. Internal nodes, edges, handles and pointer targets are clipped; exposed boundary controls remain accessible. Workspace title bars belong to View representations (including glyph-shaped artwork), not a terminal Glyph.\n\nA View may render glyph-shaped artwork without being an icon View. It is still a View representation. Every authored Surface starts with at least one View and ends in its ordinary Glyph; the terminal Glyph does not replace the View."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-view",
          "nodeId": "view-representations"
        }
      }
    },
